183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (While the MGECJ project focused on policy and rights, the SAFE project was designed to address the immediate economic precarity of our target communities. In climate hotspots like the middle belt of Ghana, up to 70% of households rely on unstable rain-fed subsistence farming. The SAFE project aims to introduce beekeeping and honey production as an alternative, climate-resilient income source. Beekeeping requires minimal land, provides income during dry seasons when crops fail, and boosts local biodiversity through pollination service.)
/E (While the MGECJ project focused on policy and rights, the SAFE project was designed to address the immediate economic precarity of our target communities. In climate hotspots like the middle belt of Ghana, up to 70% of households rely on unstable rain-fed subsistence farming. The SAFE project aims to introduce beekeeping and honey production as an alternative, climate-resilient income source. Beekeeping requires minimal land, provides income during dry seasons when crops fail, and boosts local biodiversity through pollination service.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
