186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The first phase of the SAFE project focused on technical skills transfer. We successfully identified training venues and mobilized community participants, targeting a cohort of 20 individuals, specifically prioritizing youth and women. The curriculum covered sustainable colony management, harvesting techniques, and safety protocols. By equipping participants with these skills, we are ensuring that the apiaries are managed professionally, maximizing honey yields and ensuring the longevity of the enterprise.)
/E (The first phase of the SAFE project focused on technical skills transfer. We successfully identified training venues and mobilized community participants, targeting a cohort of 20 individuals, specifically prioritizing youth and women. The curriculum covered sustainable colony management, harvesting techniques, and safety protocols. By equipping participants with these skills, we are ensuring that the apiaries are managed professionally, maximizing honey yields and ensuring the longevity of the enterprise.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Aligning with our "Knowledge Diplomacy" pillar, the SAFE project includes a research component titled "Gendered Impacts of Beekeeping Adoption on Household Income in Climate Vulnerable Communities". Data collection for this study is on track. This research aims to quantify exactly how alternative livelihood interventions impact the financial autonomy of rural women, providing the necessary data to justify scaling this model to other districts.)
/E (Aligning with our "Knowledge Diplomacy" pillar, the SAFE project includes a research component titled "Gendered Impacts of Beekeeping Adoption on Household Income in Climate Vulnerable Communities". Data collection for this study is on track. This research aims to quantify exactly how alternative livelihood interventions impact the financial autonomy of rural women, providing the necessary data to justify scaling this model to other districts.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (To translate training into economic value, IPA-GH facilitated the physical establishment of the pilot apiary. This involved the procurement and installation of 10 beehives, 10 hive stands, 8 roofing sheets, and essential protective gear including 2 bee suits, 2 smokers, and 3 pairs of gloves. The logistical execution included site clearing, transportation of equipment to remote rural locations, and the engagement of local labourers to assist in the setup. This activity successfully moved the project from concept to physical reality, providing the community with a tangible asset base.)
/E (To translate training into economic value, IPA-GH facilitated the physical establishment of the pilot apiary. This involved the procurement and installation of 10 beehives, 10 hive stands, 8 roofing sheets, and essential protective gear including 2 bee suits, 2 smokers, and 3 pairs of gloves. The logistical execution included site clearing, transportation of equipment to remote rural locations, and the engagement of local labourers to assist in the setup. This activity successfully moved the project from concept to physical reality, providing the community with a tangible asset base.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
