193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (In the community of Sankpala, identified as a high-climate hotspot in the Northern Region, the prevailing story on the ground is one of resilience stifled by systemic exclusion. The central challenge faced by residents, particularly the female farmers who secure the community's food supply, is the struggle to manage intensifying resource scarcity while battling traditional gender norms that limit their public voice. Although these women hold critical, centuries-old indigenous knowledge regarding drought-resistant crops and water management strategies, they have historically been culturally conditioned to remain silent during community decision-making processes. )
/E (In the community of Sankpala, identified as a high-climate hotspot in the Northern Region, the prevailing story on the ground is one of resilience stifled by systemic exclusion. The central challenge faced by residents, particularly the female farmers who secure the community's food supply, is the struggle to manage intensifying resource scarcity while battling traditional gender norms that limit their public voice. Although these women hold critical, centuries-old indigenous knowledge regarding drought-resistant crops and water management strategies, they have historically been culturally conditioned to remain silent during community decision-making processes. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
endobj
