/T (In Northern Ghana, traditional gender norms and cultural expectations frequently restrict women's participation in public forums, often causing them to remain silent during broader community gatherings and policy discussions. Although these women, particularly farmers, possess vital indigenous knowledge regarding food security and climate adaptation, this systemic exclusion historically marginalizes their voices, leaving their expertise underrepresented in national environmental policy-making.)
