/T (To enforce this conduct, IPA-GH utilized a dynamic risk register to identify and mitigate potential safeguarding issues, such as language barriers that could lead to exclusion or misinterpretation. We proactively engaged local interpreters and produced workshop learning materials in local languages, ensuring that no participant was left vulnerable due to a lack of understanding. This level of care allowed us to bridge the gap between marginalised rural communities and national policymakers, transforming a baseline of zero engagement into a robust and safe network for advocacy.)
